      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I've now tested and confirmed this also applies to Unity ScaleConstraints as well.  It also only occurs in VR, putting the problem somewhere in the VR interface for the hands \n\n(Is there some inverse of the scale-down for the head in play to always force the scaling on them to 1 now that needs adjusting perhaps?)\n\nThis is something that's happened due to some recent client change, as scaling hands down used to work just fine with one of my older avatars.",
